  "notes": [
    "Additional J3/CAM1 pins are recommendations requiring explicit inclusion in reconstruction; pin_types above intentionally covers only existing native logical pins.",
    "Exact ST module schematic assigns all four extra connector power contacts 31-34 to GND. Native J3 footprint already numbers its four corresponding copper contacts 31-34, but logical pins are absent. Hirose reference drawing labels the features power contacts without numerical pad IDs; their permutation is electrically immaterial only when all are GND.",
    "CAM1 pins 15,17,22,24 retain generic connector position names in native data but are NC within exact CAM-5G0-079CLR module, just as pins19/21 are. Connector J3 contacts themselves remain passive.",
    "U5 IQ order code fixes QE=1, disabling WP/HOLD pin functions; IO2/IO3 names avoid implying usable control inputs. WSON has no dedicated reset pin. Native EP9 is a footprint convention, not a manufacturer-numbered signal; package center metal has no internal signal connection and may float or connect GND.",
    "U6 R/B# pin7 is an open-drain output, represented by KiCad open_collector token. PT38 is input. VCC1/VSS1 remain power_in because manufacturer recommends their power/ground connections even where not internally bonded.",
    "J2 native Datasheet URL is for TC2070-IDC-NL and should be replaced with archived exact TC2030-IDC-NL document metadata. Three footprint pad IDs None are NPTH alignment holes, not extra electrical terminals.",
    "This is no signoff of J3 signal orientation, pad geometry, or board routing. J3 cached lands differ from Hirose recommended land widths and lengths; keep footprint manufacturing review open.",
    "Native net fragments are not authoritative complete networks; preserve reconciled EDIF/native connectivity separately from these verified pin identities."
  ]
